export const HADITH=[
[1,"Actions Are by Intentions","Actions are only by intentions, and every person will have only what they intended.","One deed can be worship or habit depending on the heart behind it. Intention is the switch that turns ordinary life — work, driving, providing — into reward.","Before one routine task today (a shift task, a school drop-off), pause and set an intention: 'This is for Allah, to care for what He entrusted to me.'"],
[2,"Islam, Iman, Ihsan","Jibril came and asked the Prophet ﷺ about Islam (the five pillars), Iman (the six beliefs), and Ihsan: 'To worship Allah as though you see Him, for though you do not see Him, He sees you.'","The deen has three floors: body (Islam), heart (Iman), and excellence (Ihsan). Ihsan is the goal — living watched.","In one salah today, pray as if you can see Him. Slow down just that one."],
[3,"Built on Five","Islam is built upon five: testimony of faith, salah, zakah, hajj, and fasting Ramadan.","These are the load-bearing walls. Strengthen the pillars before decorating the house.","Audit yourself honestly: which pillar is weakest right now? Write one step to fix it."],
[4,"Deeds Are by Endings","Your creation was decreed in stages, and deeds are judged by their endings.","No arrogance about your good state, no despair about your past. The race isn't over — finish strong.","Make du'a: 'O Turner of hearts, keep my heart firm on Your deen.'"],
[5,"No Innovation","Whoever introduces into this matter of ours what is not from it, it is rejected.","Worship is received, not invented. Sincerity needs correctness to count.","Pick one practice you do and verify its source — knowing why builds conviction."],
[6,"Halal Is Clear","The halal is clear and the haram is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever avoids the doubtful protects his deen and honor.","This is your halal-screening principle applied to everything — the grey zone is where most people slip.","Identify one 'grey area' in your life (income, entertainment, dealings) and resolve it."],
[7,"The Deen Is Sincerity","The deen is naseehah — sincerity toward Allah, His Book, His Messenger, the leaders, and the common Muslims.","Faith isn't private self-improvement; it's sincere goodwill toward everyone around you.","Give one person sincere, kind advice today — or receive some without defensiveness."],
[8,"Sanctity","I have been commanded to fight until people testify... and their blood and wealth are protected.","A Muslim's life, wealth, and honor are sacred. Honor includes not backbiting them.","Guard your tongue from one conversation about someone who isn't present."],
[9,"Do What You Can","What I have forbidden you, avoid. What I have commanded you, do as much as you can.","Prohibitions are absolute; commands flex with capacity. Allah doesn't burden beyond ability — but 'as much as you can' means actually trying.","Find your 'can': if you can't pray sunnah after a 12-hour shift, pray two instead of zero."],
[10,"Pure Income, Answered Du'a","Allah is pure and accepts only what is pure... then he mentioned the traveler raising his hands — but his food is haram, his drink is haram — how can he be answered?","Halal earnings aren't just fiqh, they're the plumbing of answered du'a.","You already screen your investments — today, thank Allah for that habit and make du'a right after a halal meal."],
[11,"Leave the Doubt","Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt.","The heart has a built-in warning system. When something feels off, that unease is data.","Next time you hesitate over a decision today, treat the hesitation as a signal — pause and check."],
[12,"Mind Your Business","From the excellence of a person's Islam is leaving what does not concern him.","Half of spiritual clutter is other people's affairs — feeds, drama, news you can't act on.","Cut 15 minutes of scrolling today and give it to one Quran page."],
[13,"Love for Your Brother","None of you truly believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself.","Envy inverts this hadith. The cure for hasad in your own heart is actively wanting good for others.","Make du'a for someone to receive the exact thing you want most."],
[14,"Life Is Sacred","The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except in three cases prescribed by law.","Human life is the heaviest thing in the scale. This extends to never treating harm casually.","Reflect: your RT work preserves the sanctity of life daily. Renew that intention."],
[15,"Speak Good or Be Silent","Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent, honor his neighbor, and honor his guest.","Three tests of faith: the tongue, the neighbor, the guest. Silence is a valid answer.","In one heated moment today (work, road, home), choose silence over the comeback."],
[16,"Do Not Get Angry","A man asked for advice. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not get angry.' He repeated the question; the answer stayed the same.","Anger is the door most regret walks through — including parking lot arguments. Not suppressing feeling, but refusing to let it drive.","Learn the protocol: when angry, say a'udhu billah, change position (stand→sit), make wudu."],
[17,"Excellence in Everything","Allah has prescribed ihsan in all things.","Excellence isn't reserved for worship — how you chart at work, how you code, how you park. All of it can be done beautifully.","Do one mundane task today at deliberately high quality, as worship."],
[18,"Follow Bad with Good","Fear Allah wherever you are, follow a bad deed with a good deed and it will erase it, and treat people with good character.","The whole deen in three lines: taqwa with Allah, repair with deeds, beauty with people.","If you slip today, don't spiral — immediately do a good deed to erase it. That's the system."],
[19,"Be Mindful of Allah","Be mindful of Allah and He will protect you. If you ask, ask Allah. Know that if the whole nation gathered to harm you, they could not — except by what Allah has written.","This is the antidote to fearing envious people. Protection is a transaction: guard His limits, He guards you.","Memorize the line: 'If the whole nation gathered to harm you...' — carry it into tense moments."],
[20,"Modesty","If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.","Haya (modesty/shame before Allah) is the internal brake. When it dies, everything is permitted.","Ask before one action today: 'Would I do this if I remembered He's watching?' (Ihsan again.)"],
[21,"Then Be Steadfast","Say: 'I believe in Allah' — then be steadfast.","Istiqamah beats intensity. Not the person who prays all night once, but the one who never misses Fajr.","Protect your smallest consistent habit today. Don't break the chain."],
[22,"The Path Is Enough","A man asked: if I pray the obligatory, fast Ramadan, treat halal as halal and haram as haram, and add nothing — will I enter Paradise? He ﷺ said: Yes.","The bar for Paradise is mercy, not perfection. Extras are love, not entry requirements. This kills religious burnout.","Release perfectionism today. Do the fard well; let that be enough for now."],
[23,"Purity Is Half of Faith","Purity is half of faith, alhamdulillah fills the scale, and the Quran is a proof for you or against you.","Every wudu is worship. And the Quran question: is it currently evidence for you or against you?","Make wudu once today slowly, with presence, knowing sins fall with the water."],
[24,"O My Servants","Hadith Qudsi: O My servants, I have forbidden oppression upon Myself, so do not oppress one another... O My servants, it is only your deeds I record for you, then I repay you for them.","Allah forbade dhulm on Himself. Every injustice you suffer is seen and will be repaid — the parking lot included.","Hand one grievance over: 'O Allah, You saw it. I leave it with You.'"],
[25,"Dhikr Levels the Field","The poor companions said: the wealthy took all the rewards — they pray as we pray but give charity from surplus wealth. He ﷺ said: every tasbih is charity, every takbir is charity...","Dhikr is the currency everyone can mint. No wealth required for a full scale.","100x SubhanAllah on the commute. It costs nothing and weighs everything."],
[26,"Every Joint Owes Charity","Every joint of a person owes charity daily: justice between two is charity, helping a man onto his mount is charity, a good word is charity, every step to prayer is charity, removing harm from the road is charity.","Your body is a debt; small kindnesses are the payment plan. Charity was never only money.","Pay today's installment: one good word, one small help, one harm removed."],
[27,"Consult Your Heart","Righteousness is good character, and sin is what wavers in your chest and you would hate for people to discover.","You carry a fatwa machine in your ribcage. The thing you'd hide is the thing to examine.","One honest self-check: what am I currently doing that I'd minimize if asked about it?"],
[28,"Hold the Rope","I advise you with taqwa, and hearing and obeying... hold firmly to my sunnah and the sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs — bite onto it with your molars.","'Bite with the molars' — the sunnah is kept through grip, especially when the environment pulls the other way.","Revive one small sunnah today: right side first, saying salam fully, eating with three fingers' worth of gratitude."],
[29,"Guard This","Mu'adh asked about entering Paradise. The Prophet ﷺ listed the pillars, then the gates of good — fasting, charity, night prayer — then grabbed his own tongue: 'Restrain this. Is there anything that throws people on their faces into the Fire except the harvest of their tongues?'","After all the great deeds, the final warning was the tongue. It undoes what everything else builds.","One day, one rule: no complaint, no mockery, no backbite. Watch how hard — and clarifying — it is."],
[30,"The Boundaries","Allah has set obligations, so do not neglect them; set limits, so do not transgress them; forbidden things, so do not violate them; and stayed silent about things as mercy — so do not dig into them.","The deen has a defined API: requirements, limits, and merciful silence. Don't invent restrictions Allah never made.","Notice one thing today that's simply permissible — and enjoy it as a mercy, guilt-free."],
[31,"True Zuhd","Be detached from the dunya and Allah will love you; be detached from what people possess and people will love you.","Zuhd isn't poverty — it's the dunya in your hand, not your heart. And ignoring what others have is the social version: the end of comparison.","Unfollow, mute, or skip one comparison trigger today."],
[32,"No Harm","There should be neither harm nor reciprocating harm.","Four words that govern all dealings — business, neighbors, family, the road. You don't initiate damage and you don't escalate it.","De-escalate one friction today. Absorb it; that's strength, not weakness."],
[33,"Proof and Oath","If people were given according to their claims, men would claim the wealth and blood of others. The burden of proof is on the claimant, and the oath on the one who denies.","Islam built due process into its DNA. Accusations — like the one thrown at you — require evidence. This is the divine standard.","Apply it inward: don't assume motives about anyone today without proof."],
[34,"Change It","Whoever sees an evil, let him change it with his hand; if unable, with his tongue; if unable, with his heart — and that is the weakest of faith.","A three-tier response protocol. Even when powerless, the heart's refusal to normalize wrong is still faith.","Identify your tier in one situation today — and act at the level you actually have."],
[35,"Brothers","Do not envy one another, inflate prices against one another, hate one another, turn away from one another... Be, O servants of Allah, brothers. Taqwa is here — and he pointed to his chest three times.","The community's diseases named in one list — envy first. And the location of piety: not appearance, the chest.","Judge one person today by less than you usually do. Taqwa is hidden; assume the best."],
[36,"Relieve and Be Relieved","Whoever relieves a believer of a hardship, Allah relieves him of a hardship on the Day of Judgment... Allah helps the servant as long as the servant helps his brother. Whoever travels a path seeking knowledge, Allah eases his path to Paradise.","Divine reciprocity: your help triggers His help. And your deen study tonight? It's literally paving your road to Jannah.","Relieve one hardship today — cover a task, ease a debt, solve someone's stuck problem."],
[37,"The Multiplication","Whoever intends a good deed and doesn't do it, Allah records it as one complete good deed. If he does it, it is recorded ten to seven hundred times over. An evil deed intended but left — recorded as a good deed.","The most generous accounting system ever written. The math is rigged in your favor.","Intend three good deeds right now. You just earned three rewards — now go collect the multiplier."],
[38,"Until I Love Him","Hadith Qudsi: My servant draws near to Me with nothing more beloved than what I made obligatory, and continues drawing near with voluntary deeds until I love him. When I love him, I am his hearing, his sight, his hand...","The ceiling of the deen: divine love, earned by fard first, then nawafil. Guidance in every limb follows.","Add one voluntary act today — two rak'ahs of duha, one extra page — as a step toward being loved."],
[39,"The Pardon","Allah has pardoned my ummah for mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they are coerced into.","The deen is not a trap. Honest error carries no sin. This should end scrupulous anxiety about accidents.","Forgive yourself for one honest mistake you've been carrying. Allah already did."],
[40,"A Stranger Passing Through","Be in this world as if you were a stranger or a traveler. When evening comes, do not expect morning; when morning comes, do not expect evening.","A traveler packs light, doesn't renovate the hotel, and keeps moving toward home. Urgency without panic.","Do one thing today you'd regret leaving undone — a call, an apology, a sadaqah."],
[41,"Aligned Desires","None of you truly believes until his desires follow what I have brought.","The final stage of faith: not just obeying reluctantly, but wanting what He ﷺ taught. Preferences reshaped.","Notice one command you follow grudgingly. Ask Allah to make you love it."],
[42,"The Ocean of Forgiveness","Hadith Qudsi: O son of Adam, were your sins to reach the clouds of the sky and you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you... were you to come to Me with sins nearly the size of the earth, not associating anything with Me, I would meet you with forgiveness the same size.","The last hadith of the collection is the door that never closes. Whatever the past holds, it fits inside this.","End tonight with 100x astaghfirullah — and mean the freedom it buys."]
];
